# Kinescope

> Kinescope is a video hosting and streaming platform for businesses, online schools and development teams. Founded in 2014, it bundles DRM (Widevine + FairPlay), a white-label player, analytics, live streaming, a REST API with 8 SDKs, an MCP server for AI agents and its own global CDN. Plans start free, then from €10/month plus pay-as-you-go usage (delivery and storage from €0.03/GB, processing €0.01/min), with no per-seat fees and no annual contracts. Trusted by 9,500+ clients in 84 countries; 99.98% monthly uptime target, backed by a financial SLA on the Mega plan.

## Key facts
- Category: secure video hosting, streaming, DRM, video API/CDN — an all-in-one video platform (not a consumer tool).
- DRM: Widevine + FairPlay included on every paid plan from €10/month (not an enterprise-only add-on), plus dynamic watermarks, signed links and domain restrictions. The Free plan has no DRM.
- Pricing: Free plan (store up to 100 min of video + 200 GB of monthly traffic, no card); Super from €10/month with unlimited storage and bandwidth — delivery from €0.03/GB down to €0.01/GB with volume, storage from €0.03/GB per month, processing €0.01/min; Mega is custom. No per-seat fees.
- Infrastructure: own global CDN (does not resell AWS/Cloudflare) across Latin America, the US, Europe and the CIS; RTMP, RTMPS and SRT ingest; HLS, DASH, CMAF and LL-HLS delivery; up to 4K.
- Developers: REST API, 8 SDKs (JavaScript IFrame Player API, React, React Native, Vue, Angular, Flutter, iOS/Swift, Android/Kotlin), 7 webhook events, an MCP server (public beta) for AI agents; SSO on the Mega plan.
- Company: Kinescope B.V., Emmen, the Netherlands; data stored in EU data centres by default; GDPR-compliant.

